      concept('Systemd', 'Systemd manages units, dependencies, startup targets, services, timers, and logs on many distributions.', 'systemctl status and journalctl inspect why a service failed before restart.', 'restarting repeatedly without reading unit logs'),
      concept('Boot process', 'Firmware starts a bootloader, which loads the kernel and initramfs before the init system starts user-space services.', 'a missing root filesystem driver is investigated in initramfs and kernel messages.', 'blaming a login shell for failure before the kernel loads'),
      concept('Kernel and modules', 'The kernel manages hardware and core resources; loadable modules add drivers and features with parameters and compatibility requirements.', 'lsmod and modprobe inspect and load a supported network driver.', 'installing an unrelated user-space package for every hardware failure')
